---
import { demoTabs } from '../data/content';
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
  <SectionHead id="demo-title" eyebrow="demo" title="See it in action">
    <p class="section-lead">
      Every prompt becomes a short lesson. The agent shows you how to say it in clear English, then does the task as if
      you had written the better prompt.
    </p>
  </SectionHead>
  <div class="tablist demo-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Demo scenarios" data-tabs>
    {
      demoTabs.map((label, index) => (
        <button
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          class="tab"
          id={`demo-tab-${index}`}
          aria-selected={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
          aria-controls={`demo-panel-${index}`}
          tabindex={index === 0 ? 0 : -1}
        >
          {label}
        </button>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <div class="window chat">
    <div class="window-bar chat-bar"><span class="t-warm">✻</span>Claude Code<span>engly · light</span></div>

    <div class="chat-body" role="tabpanel" id="demo-panel-0" aria-labelledby="demo-tab-0" tabindex="0">
      <div class="chat-prompt">
        <span class="t-mut">&gt; </span>arregla el bug del login que no deja entrar cuando el password tiene espacios
      </div>
      <div class="chat-engly">
        <span class="ln">┌ ✨ Engly</span>
        <span class="ln">│ <span class="t-fg">Better: "Fix the login bug that blocks users when the password contains spaces."</span></span>
        <span class="ln">└</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chat-agent">
        <span class="ln"><span class="t-fg">●</span> Reading src/auth/login.ts…</span>
        <span class="ln"><span class="t-fg">●</span> The validator rejects passwords with whitespace. Updating it…</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="chat-body" role="tabpanel" id="demo-panel-1" aria-labelledby="demo-tab-1" tabindex="0" hidden>
      <div class="chat-prompt">
        <span class="t-mut">&gt; </span>make that the function return the users who has more than 3 orders
      </div>
      <div class="chat-engly">
        <span class="ln">┌ ✨ Engly</span>
        <span class="ln">│ <span class="t-fg">• "make that the function return" → "make the function return"</span></span>
        <span class="ln">│ <span class="t-fg">• "users who has" → "users who have" <span class="t-mut">(plural subject)</span></span></span>
        <span class="ln">│ <span class="t-fg">Better: "Make the function return users with more than 3 orders."</span></span>
        <span class="ln">└</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chat-agent">
        <span class="ln"><span class="t-fg">●</span> Updating getUsers() to filter by order count…</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="chat-body" role="tabpanel" id="demo-panel-2" aria-labelledby="demo-tab-2" tabindex="0" hidden>
      <div class="chat-prompt"><span class="t-mut">&gt; </span>Add a loading spinner to the checkout button.</div>
      <div class="chat-engly">
        <span class="ln">┌ ✨ Engly</span>
        <span class="ln">│ <span class="t-ok">✓ Correct English.</span></span>
        <span class="ln">└</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chat-agent">
        <span class="ln"><span class="t-fg">●</span> Adding a spinner to CheckoutButton while the request is pending…</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
